{% comment %}
  Appx — Product Specs Table. Storefront app block; renders the spec table assigned to the
  current product.

  - Resolves the assigned template metaobject `spec` in TWO tiers (feature 43, data-model §9);
    the disjoint ACTIVE set guarantees <=1 table per product:
      1. `snippets/spec-table-resolve.liquid` reads `shop.metafields["$app"].routing.value` and
         emits the matched template HANDLE (or nothing, incl. products in `excludedProductGids`);
         the handle resolves via `metaobjects["$app:appx_spec_table"][handle]` (raw-handle lookup,
         proven live). Single-product assignments arrive as `routing.byProduct` entries.
      2. No match -> `spec` stays blank -> nothing renders.
    🚫 The per-product `metaobject_reference` metafield tier (features 34/35) was REMOVED
    2026-08-04 with its definition. Do not reinstate the read without reinstating the definition
    in `shopify.app.toml` — a metafield with no definition resolves to nil and the branch is dead.
  - `.status`/`.rows` read as `.status.value` / `.rows.value` (json -> array). SECTION_HEADER rows
    span both columns; DATA rows are label/value pairs, rendered via `spec-table-value.liquid`.
  - `hideWhenEmpty` is a WHOLE-CELL character test: the row is skipped when the flag is set and the
    resolved cell has zero non-whitespace characters. `strip_html` drops `<br>`s first so
    LINE_BREAKs never count. Author-entered text is escaped in the snippet; the captured cell is
    emitted unfiltered because it is already escaped and may contain `<br>`.
  - Silent by design: a non-ACTIVE status, no assigned template, or no rows renders NOTHING.
  - CONTENT-FREE TABLES render nothing either (feature 74). Two render-time gates, mirrored in the
    admin preview renderer:
      R1 a SECTION_HEADER whose label is blank after `strip` is skipped (an empty one paints a bare
         grey band with nothing in it).
      R2 if NO row survives its gate, no wrapper is emitted — not an empty <div>, not an empty
         <table> (e.g. the editor's starter scaffold resolves to nothing).
    R2 is why the body is built into `table_body` via `capture` FIRST and the wrapper decided after:
    a data cell's emptiness is undecidable without rendering it against the live product. NOT gated:
    a section header with a real label whose rows are all hidden still renders (feature 74 "R3").

  CSS lives in assets/spec-table.css, loaded via the schema "stylesheet" attribute — theme app
  extension blocks cannot use the {% stylesheet %} tag.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  Tier 1 — shop routing map. Resolve a template handle from the product's attributes, then look up
  its metaobject by handle. The resolver emits nothing for an excluded / unmatched product, so
  `spec` stays blank (tier 2).

  Feature 108 (metaobject sharding): the two per-product maps (`byProduct` / `excluded`) live in
  per-bucket shard metaobjects keyed by `product.id mod N`, not the `$app:routing` metafield. We
  resolve THIS product's single shard here and pass it into the resolver alongside `routing`,
  keeping the snippet a pure function of its inputs.

  🔴 The `modulo: 1024` literal and the `$app:appx_routing_shard` type string are a CROSS-LANGUAGE
  CONTRACT with `ROUTING_SHARD_COUNT` / `ROUTING_SHARD_TYPE` in app/utils/routingShards.ts — they
  MUST match, and `routingShardWireContract.test.ts` reads this file off disk and fails if they
  drift. A bucket with no shard resolves `shard` to nil, treated as a clean miss.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign routing = shop.metafields["$app"].routing.value
  assign shard_key = product.id | modulo: 1024
  assign shard_handle = "routing-shard-" | append: shard_key
  assign shard = metaobjects["$app:appx_routing_shard"][shard_handle]
-%}
{%- capture routed_handle -%}{%- render "spec-table-resolve", product: product, routing: routing, shard: shard -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Shopify wraps app-extension snippet output in `<!-- BEGIN/END app snippet -->` comments;
  strip_html removes those (and any stray tags), then strip trims whitespace. A metaobject handle
  has no HTML characters, so strip_html is lossless here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign routed_handle = routed_handle | strip_html | strip -%}
{%- if routed_handle != blank -%}
  {%- assign spec = metaobjects["$app:appx_spec_table"][routed_handle] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rows = spec.rows.value
  assign styling_css = spec.styling_css.value
  assign styling = spec.styling.value
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Collapsible sections (feature 57 Step 9a). These two knobs are the ONLY ones Liquid reads from
  the raw `styling` field rather than the precomputed `styling_css`, deliberately: they are MARKUP
  decisions (`<details>` and its `open` attribute), not part of the CSS mapping, so Step 7's "the
  server precomputes; Liquid only prints" rule is not violated — just two scalars.

  The wire is OVERRIDES-ONLY, which frees this of defaulting logic: a default-styled template has no
  `sectionsCollapsible` key, so the lookup is nil (falsy — the correct `false` default with zero
  code). Same for the initial state via `| default:`.

  ⚠️ THAT `| default:` MUST TRACK `DEFAULT_SECTIONS_INITIAL_STATE` in app/utils/tableStyling.ts. A
  mismatch is SILENT — admin preview and storefront would disagree about which sections start open,
  on exactly the templates that store no value. Enforced despite Liquid being outside the module
  graph: `specTableLiquidDefaultsContract.test.ts` reads this file off disk and compares the literal
  below to the domain constant. Collapsible degrades to the flat shape when the template has no
  section headers, matching the admin preview renderer exactly.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign section_rows = rows | where: "rowType", "SECTION_HEADER"
  assign collapsible = false
  if styling.sectionsCollapsible and section_rows.size > 0
    assign collapsible = true
  endif
  assign initial_state = styling.sectionsInitialState | default: "FIRST_OPEN"
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Styling (feature 57 Step 7). `styling_css` is PRECOMPUTED server-side at sync time — `.classes`
  is the space-joined BEM modifier list, `.vars` the `--appx-spec-*: v;` declarations — so this
  template performs NO styling logic and needs no change when a knob is added. The mapping lives once
  in `app/utils/tableStylingCss.ts`, shared with the admin preview (data-model §10). An entry synced
  before this field existed leaves both blank (renders as pre-Step-7; self-heals on the next save).
  `escape` is defense in depth only: values are whitelist-validated upstream at `parseStylingValues`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if spec != blank and spec.status.value == "ACTIVE" and rows != blank and rows.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Feature 74 — R2. The body is CAPTURED, then the wrapper emitted only if something rendered.
    `has_content` is assigned inside the capture and read after it: `capture` redirects OUTPUT, not
    assignments, so the flag (like `table_open` / `details_open` / `section_index`) survives the
    block. The capture is why this works in one pass — a DATA row's emptiness depends on the live
    product, so a pre-pass "will anything render?" would render every value cell twice.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign has_content = false -%}
  {%- capture table_body -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      TWO markup shapes, switched by `collapsible`, sharing ONE row loop so the hideWhenEmpty gate
      can never differ:
      - OFF (default): one <table>, section headers as full-width <tr>. Byte-for-byte what shipped
        before Step 9a — must not move.
      - ON: one <details> per section header, each wrapping its OWN <table>. Rows BEFORE the first
        section header render in a leading bare <table> (no section to name), so `table_open` opens
        lazily. A section whose rows are all hidden renders as an empty collapsible (no new emptiness
        logic). Each per-section table carries an aria-label with the title (the split costs it the
        <th scope="colgroup"> heading). No JavaScript: <details> is native and keyboard-operable.

      EXPLICIT ARIA ROLES (feature 70) restate semantics the tags already express, because the
      STACKED layouts apply `display: block`, dropping the element out of the CSS table model and
      taking the browser's implicit table semantics with it. Roles are immune to `display`.
      UNCONDITIONAL on purpose: the mobile stacked rule is a MEDIA QUERY, and Liquid renders
      server-side with no idea of screen width, so a role emitted only when `rowLayout == STACKED`
      would leave every narrow-screen shopper of a two-column template broken. ALL OR NOTHING:
      table -> rowgroup -> row -> rowheader/cell must stay complete (a partial chain can be dropped
      outright by AT). `specTableAriaContract.test.ts` fails if one goes missing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if collapsible -%}
      {%- assign table_open = false -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table"><tbody role="rowgroup">
      {%- assign table_open = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign details_open = false -%}
    {%- assign section_index = 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify caps for-loops at 50 iterations; templates hold up to MAX_TEMPLATE_ROWS (200) rows,
      so iterate in 50-row chunks.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign row_chunks = rows.size | plus: 49 | divided_by: 50 -%}
    {%- for chunk in (1..row_chunks) -%}
      {%- assign row_offset = chunk | minus: 1 | times: 50 -%}
      {%- for row in rows offset: row_offset limit: 50 -%}
        {%- if row.rowType == "SECTION_HEADER" -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            R1 (feature 74). A blank section header is skipped in BOTH shapes. Tested trimmed,
            emitted untrimmed. The filter has to land in an `assign`: Liquid `if` conditions do not
            accept filters.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign section_label = row.label | strip -%}
          {%- if collapsible -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A blank header still CLOSES the open group before vanishing — without the close, the
              rows that followed would be filed under the PREVIOUS section's heading. They hit the
              lazy-open branch below and land in a fresh bare unnamed table. `section_index` is NOT
              incremented: a skipped section is not a section, so FIRST_OPEN opens the first REAL one.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if table_open -%}</tbody></table>{%- assign table_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if details_open -%}</details>{%- assign details_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if section_label != blank -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign is_open = false
                if initial_state == "ALL_OPEN"
                  assign is_open = true
                elsif initial_state == "FIRST_OPEN" and section_index == 0
                  assign is_open = true
                endif
              -%}
              <details class="appx-spec-table__section-group"{% if is_open %} open{% endif %}>
                <summary class="appx-spec-table__section-summary">{{ row.label | escape }}</summary>
                <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table" aria-label="{{ row.label | escape }}"><tbody role="rowgroup">
              {%- liquid
                assign details_open = true
                assign table_open = true
                assign section_index = section_index | plus: 1
                assign has_content = true
              -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- if section_label != blank -%}
              <tr class="appx-spec-table__section-row" role="row">
                <th class="appx-spec-table__section" colspan="2" scope="colgroup" role="columnheader" aria-colspan="2">{{ row.label | escape }}</th>
              </tr>
              {%- assign has_content = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- capture cell -%}{% render "spec-table-value", row: row, product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- assign cell_plain = cell | strip_html | strip -%}
          {%- unless row.hideWhenEmpty and cell_plain == blank -%}
            {%- unless table_open -%}
              <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table"><tbody role="rowgroup">
              {%- assign table_open = true -%}
            {%- endunless -%}
            <tr class="appx-spec-table__row" role="row">
              <th class="appx-spec-table__label" scope="row" role="rowheader">{{ row.label | escape }}</th>
              <td class="appx-spec-table__value" role="cell">{{ cell }}</td>
            </tr>
            {%- assign has_content = true -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if table_open -%}</tbody></table>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if details_open -%}</details>{%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `table_body` is printed RAW: Liquid does not auto-escape, and every author-entered string inside
    it was escaped at emission time. When nothing rendered, the captured body (which may still hold
    an empty <table><tbody></tbody></table> from the flat shape's eager open) is simply discarded.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_content -%}
    <div class="appx-spec-table {{ styling_css.classes | escape }}" style="{{ styling_css.vars | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ table_body }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product specs table",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "spec-table.css",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
